hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18984","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Mughirah informed us, from Shibak, from Amir, So-and-so al-Thaqafi informed me, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about three things, and he did not permit us any of them: We asked him to return Abu Bakrah to us, and he was a slave who had embraced Islam before us, and he said: No, he is the freedman of Allah, then the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then we asked him to permit us in winter, and our land was a cold land, meaning in purification, and he did not permit us. And we asked him to permit us in gourds, and he did not permit us therein."
